00:16:07.270 --> 00:16:11.880
However, if those data do
not reflect the real world,

00:16:11.880 --> 00:16:14.080
it doesn't make any sense.

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:17.560
It doesn't won't work
in the real world.

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:23.370
So the question is, how you can
detect such a silly situation,

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:27.960
how you can avoid it, how you
can mitigate the situation.

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:31.210
That is continuous deployment.

00:16:31.210 --> 00:16:35.160
So to explain and to make
the scenario a little bit

00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:38.280
interesting, I would
have some assumption.

00:16:38.280 --> 00:16:43.710
Now, suppose that they keep
collecting data every day.

00:16:43.710 --> 00:16:48.090
On the first day, day one, how
much just 0's, unfortunately.

00:16:48.090 --> 00:16:52.290
But next day, they
